# ============================================================
# Sprout — environment configuration
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env` in the SAME folder and fill in the values.
# `.env` is gitignored and must never be committed. This file holds
# key names only, never a real token.
#
#     copy .env.example .env      (Windows)
#     cp   .env.example .env      (macOS / Linux)
#
# Nothing here is required for the app to run. The ML forecasts,
# What-If simulator, scenario comparison and every chart work with no
# .env file at all — only the AI-written explanation needs a key, and
# it falls back to a locally-generated explanation when there isn't one.
# ============================================================

# --- Hugging Face (AI interpretation layer) -----------------
# Get a token at: https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens
# Create a *fine-grained* token with the "Inference Providers" permission.
# It looks like: hf_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
HF_API_KEY=

# The model that writes the natural-language insight. This is the
# INTERPRETATION layer only — it never produces any number. All numbers
# come from the project's own trained models (see ml/README_ML.md).
# Any chat-completion model on the HF router works; swap it freely.
#
#   meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct   - default: small, fast, widely served,
#                                        returns plain prose reliably
#   deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V3.2-Exp      - also verified working; larger/slower
#
# ⚠ AVOID REASONING MODELS HERE (openai/gpt-oss-*, zai-org/GLM-*-Air, and
# similar). They split their output into a reasoning channel and a final
# answer, and at this task's small token budget the budget is spent entirely
# on reasoning — the call returns HTTP 200 with an EMPTY message, so the app
# silently falls back to its local writer. The app detects this case and
# names it in the failure reason, but the fix is to pick a non-reasoning
# model. This task is summarising numbers that are already final, so a
# reasoning model buys nothing anyway.
#
# Note also that the router picks a provider for you, and some providers are
# region-blocked (Groq returned an HTTP 403 Cloudflare page from India during
# testing). If a model fails for you, try another one from the list above.
HF_MODEL=meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct

# OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint for the HF router.
# Only change this if you want to point the AI layer at a different
# OpenAI-compatible provider entirely.
HF_API_URL=https://router.huggingface.co/v1/chat/completions

# How long (seconds) to wait for the AI before giving up and using the
# local fallback writer. Keep this low — a slow insight is worse than an
# instant local one.
HF_TIMEOUT=20
